            text: "Physically yes, but it is not recommended. Epoxy bonds mechanically into open concrete pores, and paint covers them, so the whole system relies on the paint’s grip on the slab. Since garage floor paint typically lasts one to three years, you are building a long-lived coating on a short-lived foundation.",
          },
        },
        {
