        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you put epoxy over an existing epoxy floor?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes, and this is a much better case than painting over paint. Epoxy bonds well to epoxy provided the existing coating is sound. Scuff-sand the whole floor to dull the gloss, clean thoroughly and recoat. If the existing epoxy is peeling or blistering, it must come off first.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How long will epoxy over paint last?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Less than epoxy over properly prepared concrete, because the paint underneath sets the ceiling. A high-solids epoxy on a ground slab can give eight to twelve years; over sound paint you should plan for considerably less and budget to redo it sooner. If the paint fails, both layers lift together.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
